   Later explicit user instructions supersede this snapshot; update the documents accordingly.

Role:

- Codex is the default primary agent.
- Cursor is the backup primary agent when Codex has no quota or is unavailable.
- Work on a `cursor/<scope>-<topic>` branch; never edit `main` directly.
- Formal `05_论文/正式/` and `06_交付/` are written by Codex by default. Cursor may write `05_论文/待审/` and candidate artifacts. Writing formal artifacts requires explicit user authorization recorded in `docs/collab/decisions.md`.
- Cursor cannot resume a Codex thread. Continue from the handoff file, not by inventing missing context.

AI compliance:

- Cursor is an AI tool. Any AI-assisted text/code/formula/figure/result must follow the skill's `references/18_AI工具合规与使用报告.md`: declaration, tool reference entry, in-text/code/figure marks, and AI Tool Usage Report.
- Do not copy AI output without team verification.

Before finishing:

- Post a `reply`/`handoff` for any claimed bus message and mark it `done`; if blocked, reply with the exact blocker and keep it `claimed`.
- Run the relevant tests/audits.
- Update `docs/collab/CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` with what changed, commands/results, next steps, blockers.
- Do not overwrite another agent's uncommitted work.
